WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.740
A delivery drone takes off from
the corner of a square grid.

2
00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:07.830
First leg: three squares
east, four squares north.

3
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.920
Then a new instruction:
six east, eight north.

4
00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:15.060
At the end of the first leg,
did the drone turn a corner,

5
00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:16.830
or carry straight on?

6
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.500
The numbers changed, so surely
the direction changed too?

7
00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:24.560
Or does it fly straight only if
both legs are the same length?

8
00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:27.930
In this mission, you'll write
each leg as a column vector:

9
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.400
three on top, four underneath.

10
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:35.510
You'll add vectors nose to tail, and
multiply a vector by a number to scale it.

11
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.310
Your mission: decide whether the
drone flew in a straight line.
